{"cells": [{"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["# Hierarchical Demand Forecasting for Fashion Retail\n", "\n", "## End-to-End Multi-Horizon, Multi-Granularity Forecasting Pipeline\n", "\n", "This notebook demonstrates a comprehensive hierarchical demand forecasting solution featuring:\n", "\n", "**Multi-Horizon Forecasting**:\n", "- 24 hours (intraday)\n", "- 7 days (weekly)\n", "- 31 days (monthly)\n", "- 90 days (quarterly)\n", "- 3 months\n", "- 12 months (annual)\n", "\n", "**Hierarchy Levels**:\n", "- Country (US, UK, DE, FR, JP)\n", "- Shop (Downtown, Mall, Airport, Outlet, Online)\n", "- Product Category (Tops, Bottoms, Outerwear, Footwear, Accessories)\n", "- Product Group (T-Shirts, Jeans, Jackets, etc.)\n", "- SKU (specific product variants)\n", "- SKU Size (XS, S, M, L, XL, XXL)\n", "\n", "**Advanced Features**:\n", "- Seasonality pattern detection (daily, weekly, monthly, annual, multi)\n", "- Optimized lag feature selection using feature importance\n", "- Causal inference for leading SKU detection\n", "- Multiple SOTA models: LSTM, DeepAR, TFT, N-BEATS\n", "- Ensemble stacking (Blending)\n", "- Conformal prediction for uncertainty quantification\n", "- Hierarchical reconciliation (MinT)"]}, {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["## 1. Setup and Imports"]}, {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": null, "metadata": {}, "outputs": [], "source": ["import numpy as np\n", "import pandas as pd\n", "import warnings\n", "from pathlib import Path\n", "from typing import Dict, List, Tuple, Optional\n", "from datetime import datetime, timedelta\n", "\n", "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n", "import seaborn as sns\n", "from sklearn.ensemble import GradientBoostingRegressor, RandomForestRegressor\n", "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n", "from sklearn.metrics import mean_absolute_error, mean_squared_error, mean_absolute_percentage_error\n", "from sklearn.model_selection import TimeSeriesSplit\n", "\n", "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n", "\n", "# Set plot styles\n", "sns.set_style('whitegrid')\n", "plt.rcParams['figure.figsize'] = (14, 6)\n", "plt.rcParams['figure.dpi'] = 100\n", "\n", "print(f\"NumPy version: {np.__version__}\")\n", "print(f\"Pandas version: {pd.__version__}\")"]}, {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["## 2. Hierarchical Data Generation"]}, {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": null, "metadata": {}, "outputs": [], "source": ["def generate_hierarchical_demand_data(\n", "    n_weeks: int = 104,\n", "    seed: int = 42\n", ") -> pd.DataFrame:\n", "    \"\"\"\n", "    Generate comprehensive hierarchical demand data for fashion retail.\n", "    \n", "    Hierarchy: Country > Shop > Product Category > Product Group > SKU > SKU_Size\n", "    \"\"\"\n", "    np.random.seed(seed)\n", "    \n", "    countries = [\"US\", \"UK\", \"DE\", \"FR\", \"JP\"]\n", "    shops = [\"Downtown\", \"Mall\", \"Airport\", \"Outlet\", \"Online\"]\n", "    categories = [\"Tops\", \"Bottoms\", \"Outerwear\", \"Footwear\", \"Accessories\"]\n", "    \n", "    product_groups = {\n", "        \"Tops\": [\"T-Shirts\", \"Blouses\", \"Sweaters\", \"Hoodies\"],\n", "        \"Bottoms\": [\"Jeans\", \"Leggings\", \"Shorts\", \"Skirts\"],\n", "        \"Outerwear\": [\"Jackets\", \"Coats\", \"Vests\"],\n", "        \"Footwear\": [\"Sneakers\", \"Boots\", \"Sandals\"],\n", "        \"Accessories\": [\"Scarves\", \"Hats\", \"Belts\"],\n", "    }\n", "    \n", "    sizes = [\"XS\", \"S\", \"M\", \"L\", \"XL\", \"XXL\"]\n", "    \n", "    base_prices = {\n", "        \"Tops\": {\"T-Shirts\": 29.99, \"Blouses\": 49.99, \"Sweaters\": 59.99, \"Hoodies\": 69.99},\n", "        \"Bottoms\": {\"Jeans\": 79.99, \"Leggings\": 49.99, \"Shorts\": 39.99, \"Skirts\": 54.99},\n", "        \"Outerwear\": {\"Jackets\": 129.99, \"Coats\": 199.99, \"Vests\": 89.99},\n", "        \"Footwear\": {\"Sneakers\": 119.99, \"Boots\": 149.99, \"Sandals\": 79.99},\n", "        \"Accessories\": {\"Scarves\": 34.99, \"Hats\": 24.99, \"Belts\": 39.99},\n", "    }\n", "    \n", "    size_demand_multipliers = {\"XS\": 0.7, \"S\": 0.9, \"M\": 1.1, \"L\": 1.1, \"XL\": 0.9, \"XXL\": 0.6}\n", "    country_trend = {\"US\": 1.02, \"UK\": 1.01, \"DE\": 1.00, \"FR\": 1.01, \"JP\": 1.03}\n", "    country_seasonality_amp = {\"US\": 0.15, \"UK\": 0.12, \"DE\": 0.10, \"FR\": 0.13, \"JP\": 0.11}\n", "    \n", "    rows = []\n", "    \n", "    for week in range(1, n_weeks + 1):\n", "        day_of_year = (week * 7) % 365\n", "        week_of_year = week % 52\n", "        is_holiday = week in [8, 24, 35, 48, 52, 56, 71, 80, 88, 96]\n", "        is_back_to_school = week in [17, 18, 70, 71]\n", "        is_black_friday = week in [48, 100]\n", "        is_christmas = week in [50, 51, 52, 4]\n", "        day_of_week = (week * 7) % 7\n", "        \n", "        trend = np.prod([country_trend[c] for c in countries]) ** (week / 52)\n", "        annual_seasonality = np.sin(2 * np.pi * day_of_year / 365)\n", "        semi_annual = np.sin(4 * np.pi * day_of_year / 365)\n", "        seasonality = 1 + 0.15 * annual_seasonality + 0.08 * semi_annual\n", "        weekend_effect = 1.3 if day_of_week in [5, 6] else 1.0\n", "        \n", "        for country in countries:\n", "            country_factor = np.random.uniform(0.8, 1.2)\n", "            country_seasonal_amp = country_seasonality_amp[country]\n", "            country_seasonality = 1 + country_seasonal_amp * annual_seasonality\n", "            \n", "            for shop in shops:\n", "                shop_factor = np.random.uniform(0.7, 1.3)\n", "                \n", "                for category in categories:\n", "                    for product_group in product_groups[category]:\n", "                        group_factor = np.random.uniform(0.8, 1.2)\n", "                        base_price = base_prices.get(category, {}).get(product_group, 50.0)\n", "                        \n", "                        for sku_idx in range(4):\n", "                            sku = f\"{category[:3].upper()}-{product_group[:3].upper()}-{sku_idx:03d}\"\n", "                            \n", "                            for size in sizes:\n", "                                size_mult = size_demand_multipliers[size]\n", "                                base_demand = np.random.poisson(100)\n", "                                \n", "                                if is_black_friday:\n", "                                    discount = np.random.choice([20, 30, 40], p=[0.4, 0.4, 0.2])\n", "                                elif is_holiday:\n", "                                    discount = np.random.choice([10, 15, 20], p=[0.5, 0.3, 0.2])\n", "                                else:\n", "                                    discount = np.random.choice([0, 5, 10], p=[0.6, 0.25, 0.15])\n", "                                \n", "                                promo_effect = 1 + (discount / 50)\n", "                                holiday_effect = 1.2 if (is_christmas or is_back_to_school) else 1.0\n", "                                noise = np.random.lognormal(0, 0.2)\n", "                                \n", "                                demand = (\n", "                                    base_demand * trend * seasonality * country_seasonality *\n", "                                    country_factor * shop_factor * group_factor *\n", "                                    weekend_effect * size_mult * promo_effect * holiday_effect * noise\n", "                                )\n", "                                \n", "                                quantity = max(0, int(demand))\n", "                                revenue = quantity * base_price * (1 - discount / 100)\n", "                                \n", "                                rows.append({\n", "                                    \"week\": week,\n", "                                    \"country\": country,\n", "                                    \"shop\": shop,\n", "                                    \"product_category\": category,\n", "                                    \"product_group\": product_group,\n", "                                    \"sku\": sku,\n", "                                    \"sku_size\": size,\n", "                                    \"quantity_sold\": quantity,\n", "                                    \"revenue\": round(revenue, 2),\n", "                                    \"base_price\": base_price,\n", "                                    \"discount_pct\": discount,\n", "                                    \"is_holiday\": is_holiday,\n", "                                    \"is_back_to_school\": is_back_to_school,\n", "                                    \"is_black_friday\": is_black_friday,\n", "                                    \"is_christmas\": is_christmas,\n", "                                    \"day_of_year\": day_of_year,\n", "                                    \"week_of_year\": week_of_year,\n", "                                    \"day_of_week\": day_of_week,\n", "                                })\n", "    \n", "    df = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n", "    return df\n", "\n", "# Generate data\n", "print(\"Generating hierarchical demand data...\")\n", "df = generate_hierarchical_demand_data(n_weeks=104)\n", "print(f\"Generated {len(df):,} records\")\n", "print(f\"\\nHierarchy levels:\")\n", "print(f\"  - Countries: {df['country'].nunique()}\")\n", "print(f\"  - Shops: {df['shop'].nunique()}\")\n", "print(f\"  - Categories: {df['product_category'].nunique()}\")\n", "print(f\"  - Product Groups: {df['product_group'].nunique()}\")\n", "print(f\"  - SKUs: {df['sku'].nunique()}\")\n", "print(f\"  - Sizes: {df['sku_size'].nunique()}\")"]}, {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["## 3. Time Horizon Configuration"]}, {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": null, "metadata": {}, "outputs": [], "source": ["# Define time horizons for forecasting\n", "TIME_HORIZONS = {\n", "    \"24 hours\": {\"hours\": 24, \"days\": 1, \"weeks\": 0, \"months\": 0},\n", "    \"7 days\": {\"hours\": 168, \"days\": 7, \"weeks\": 1, \"months\": 0},\n", "    \"31 days\": {\"hours\": 744, \"days\": 31, \"weeks\": 4, \"months\": 1},\n", "    \"90 days\": {\"hours\": 2160, \"days\": 90, \"weeks\": 13, \"months\": 3},\n", "    \"3 months\": {\"hours\": 2190, \"days\": 91, \"weeks\": 13, \"months\": 3},\n", "    \"12 months\": {\"hours\": 8760, \"days\": 365, \"weeks\": 52, \"months\": 12},\n", "}\n", "\n", "# Seasonality patterns\n", "SEASONALITY_PATTERNS = [\"none\", \"daily\", \"weekly\", \"monthly\", \"quarterly\", \"annual\", \"multi\"]\n", "\n", "print(\"Available time horizons:\")\n", "for name, config in TIME_HORIZONS.items():\n", "    print(f\"  - {name}: {config['days']} days / {config['weeks']} weeks\")"]}, {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["## 4. Seasonality Detection"]}, {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": null, "metadata": {}, "outputs": [], "source": ["class SeasonalityDetector:\n", "    \"\"\"\n", "    Detect seasonality patterns in time series data.\n", "    \n", "    Identifies daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, and annual patterns using autocorrelation.\n", "    \"\"\"\n", "    \n", "    def __init__(self):\n", "        self.seasonality_patterns = {}\n", "    \n", "    def detect_seasonality(\n", "        self,\n", "        df: pd.DataFrame,\n", "        groupby_cols: List[str] = [\"country\", \"shop\", \"product_category\", \"product_group\", \"sku\", \"sku_size\"]\n", "    ) -> Dict[str, str]:\n", "        \"\"\"\n", "        Detect seasonality patterns at each hierarchy level using autocorrelation.\n", "        \"\"\"\n", "        seasonality_patterns = {}\n", "        \n", "        for _, group in df.groupby(groupby_cols, group_keys=False):\n", "            if len(group) < 52:\n", "                continue\n", "            \n", "            key = \"_\".join([str(group[col].iloc[0]) for col in groupby_cols])\n", "            ts = group.sort_values(\"week\")[\"quantity_sold\"].values\n", "            \n", "            # Calculate autocorrelation\n", "            ts_centered = ts - np.mean(ts)\n", "            autocorr = np.correlate(ts_centered, ts_centered, mode=\"full\")\n", "            autocorr = autocorr[len(autocorr) // 2:]\n", "            autocorr = autocorr / autocorr[0]\n", "            \n", "            # Find peaks in autocorrelation at different periods\n", "            peaks = []\n", "            periods_to_check = [1, 7, 14, 28, 52, 91, 182, 365]\n", "            \n", "            for period in periods_to_check:\n", "                if period < len(autocorr):\n", "                    window_start = max(0, period - 2)\n", "                    window_end = min(len(autocorr), period + 2)\n", "                    peak_value = np.max(autocorr[window_start:window_end])\n", "                    if peak_value > 0.3:\n", "                        peaks.append(period)\n", "            \n", "            # Determine dominant seasonality\n", "            if len(peaks) == 0:\n", "                pattern = \"none\"\n", "            elif 1 in peaks and 7 in peaks and 52 in peaks:\n", "                pattern = \"multi\"\n", "            elif 7 in peaks and 52 in peaks:\n", "                pattern = \"multi\"\n", "            elif 7 in peaks:\n", "                pattern = \"weekly\"\n", "            elif 1 in peaks:\n", "                pattern = \"daily\"\n", "            elif 28 in peaks or 30 in peaks:\n", "                pattern = \"monthly\"\n", "            elif 52 in peaks:\n", "                pattern = \"annual\"\n", "            elif 91 in peaks:\n", "                pattern = \"quarterly\"\n", "            else:\n", "                pattern = \"weekly\"\n", "            \n", "            seasonality_patterns[key] = pattern\n", "        \n", "        self.seasonality_patterns = seasonality_patterns\n", "        return seasonality_patterns\n", "    \n", "    def get_pattern_summary(self) -> Dict[str, int]:\n", "        \"\"\"Return summary of detected seasonality patterns.\"\"\"\n", "        summary = {}\n", "        for pattern in self.seasonality_patterns.values():\n", "            summary[pattern] = summary.get(pattern, 0) + 1\n", "        return summary\n", "\n", "# Detect seasonality\n", "print(\"Detecting seasonality patterns...\")\n", "seasonality_detector = SeasonalityDetector()\n", "sample_df = df.groupby([\"country\", \"shop\", \"product_category\", \"product_group\", \"sku\", \"sku_size\"]).head(100)\n", "seasonality_patterns = seasonality_detector.detect_seasonality(sample_df)\n", "pattern_summary = seasonality_detector.get_pattern_summary()\n", "\n", "print(\"\\nSeasonality pattern distribution:\")\n", "for pattern, count in pattern_summary.items():\n", "    print(f\"  {pattern}: {count} series\")"]}, {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["## 5. Lag Feature Selection"]}, {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": null, "metadata": {}, "outputs": [], "source": ["class LagFeatureSelector:\n", "    \"\"\"\n", "    Optimize lag feature selection using feature importance.\n", "    \n", "    Identifies the most predictive lag windows for different forecasting horizons.\n", "    \"\"\"\n", "    \n", "    def __init__(self):\n", "        self.selected_lags = {}\n", "        self.feature_importance = {}\n", "    \n", "    def select_optimal_lags(\n", "        self,\n", "        df: pd.DataFrame,\n", "        target_col: str = \"quantity_sold\",\n", "        candidate_lags: List[int] = None,\n", "        max_lags: int = 5,\n", "        horizon_type: str = \"weekly\"\n", "    ) -> List[int]:\n", "        \"\"\"\n", "        Select optimal lag features based on feature importance.\n", "        \"\"\"\n", "        if candidate_lags is None:\n", "            # Different candidate lags based on horizon\n", "            if horizon_type == \"daily\":\n", "                candidate_lags = [1, 2, 4, 6, 12, 24, 48, 72]\n", "            elif horizon_type == \"weekly\":\n", "                candidate_lags = [1, 2, 4, 7, 8, 14, 21, 28, 52]\n", "            elif horizon_type == \"monthly\":\n", "                candidate_lags = [1, 4, 8, 12, 14, 28, 30, 52, 91, 182]\n", "            else:  # quarterly/yearly\n", "                candidate_lags = [4, 8, 12, 13, 26, 52, 91, 182, 365]\n", "        \n", "        df_lagged = df.copy()\n", "        \n", "        # Create lag features\n", "        for lag in candidate_lags:\n", "            df_lagged[f\"lag_{lag}\"] = df_lagged.groupby([\"country\", \"shop\", \"product_category\", \"product_group\", \"sku\", \"sku_size\"])[\n", "                target_col\n", "            ].shift(lag)\n", "        \n", "        df_clean = df_lagged.dropna()\n", "        \n", "        if len(df_clean) < 100:\n", "            return candidate_lags[:max_lags]\n", "        \n", "        # Train model to get feature importance\n", "        feature_cols = [f\"lag_{lag}\" for lag in candidate_lags]\n", "        X = df_clean[feature_cols]\n", "        y = df_clean[target_col]\n", "        \n", "        model = GradientBoostingRegressor(n_estimators=100, random_state=42)\n", "        model.fit(X, y)\n", "        \n", "        # Get feature importance\n", "        importance = dict(zip(feature_cols, model.feature_importances_))\n", "        self.feature_importance = importance\n", "        \n", "        # Select top lags\n", "        sorted_lags = sorted(importance.keys(), key=lambda x: importance[x], reverse=True)[:max_lags]\n", "        selected_lags = [int(lag.replace(\"lag_\", \"\")) for lag in sorted_lags]\n", "        \n", "        self.selected_lags = selected_lags\n", "        return selected_lags\n", "    \n", "    def get_lag_windows(self) -> Dict[str, List[int]]:\n", "        \"\"\"Return lag windows organized by time period.\"\"\"\n", "        return {\n", "            \"short_term\": [lag for lag in self.selected_lags if lag <= 7],\n", "            \"medium_term\": [lag for lag in self.selected_lags if 7 < lag <= 31],\n", "            \"long_term\": [lag for lag in self.selected_lags if lag > 31],\n", "        }\n", "\n", "# Select optimal lags for weekly horizon\n", "print(\"Selecting optimal lag features...\")\n", "lag_selector = LagFeatureSelector()\n", "selected_lags = lag_selector.select_optimal_lags(df, max_lags=5, horizon_type=\"weekly\")\n", "print(f\"\\nSelected lags: {selected_lags}\")\n", "print(f\"\\nLag windows:\")\n", "windows = lag_selector.get_lag_windows()\n", "for window, lags in windows.items():\n", "    print(f\"  {window}: {lags}\")\n", "print(f\"\\nFeature importance:\")\n", "for lag, imp in sorted(lag_selector.feature_importance.items(), key=lambda x: x[1], reverse=True)[:5]:\n", "    print(f\"  {lag}: {imp:.4f}\")"]}, {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["## 6. Causal Inference for Leading SKU Detection"]}, {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": null, "metadata": {}, "outputs": [], "source": ["class CausalInferenceEngine:\n", "    \"\"\"\n", "    Causal inference engine for leading SKU detection using Granger causality.\n", "    \n", "    Identifies SKUs whose demand patterns predict demand at higher aggregation levels.\n", "    \"\"\"\n", "    \n", "    def __init__(self):\n", "        self.causality_scores = {}\n", "        self.leading_skus = {}\n", "    \n", "    def granger_causality_test(\n", "        self,\n", "        time_series_x: np.ndarray,\n", "        time_series_y: np.ndarray,\n", "        max_lag: int = 12\n", "    ) -> Dict[str, float]:\n", "        \"\"\"\n", "        Test if X Granger-causes Y using correlation at different lags.\n", "        \n", "        Returns causality score indicating predictive power.\n", "        \"\"\"\n", "        min_len = min(len(time_series_x), len(time_series_y))\n", "        if min_len < max_lag * 2:\n", "            return {\"score\": 0.0, \"p_value\": 1.0}\n", "        \n", "        x = time_series_x[:min_len]\n", "        y = time_series_y[:min_len]\n", "        \n", "        # Calculate correlation at different lags\n", "        scores = []\n", "        for lag in range(1, min(max_lag + 1, min_len // 2)):\n", "            x_lagged = x[lag:]\n", "            y_current = y[:-lag]\n", "            corr = np.corrcoef(x_lagged, y_current)[0, 1]\n", "            if not np.isnan(corr):\n", "                scores.append(abs(corr))\n", "        \n", "        if scores:\n", "            return {\"score\": np.mean(scores), \"p_value\": 1 - np.mean(scores)}\n", "        return {\"score\": 0.0, \"p_value\": 1.0}\n", "    \n", "    def identify_leading_skus(\n", "        self,\n", "        df: pd.DataFrame,\n", "        hierarchy_levels: List[str] = [\"product_category\", \"product_group\", \"sku\", \"sku_size\"]\n", "    ) -> Dict[str, List[str]]:\n", "        \"\"\"\n", "        Identify leading SKUs at each hierarchy level using causal inference.\n", "        \n", "        Leading SKUs are those whose demand patterns Granger-cause demand\n", "        at higher aggregation levels.\n", "        \"\"\"\n", "        leading_skus = {}\n", "        \n", "        for i in range(len(hierarchy_levels) - 1):\n", "            lower_level = hierarchy_levels[i]\n", "            upper_level = hierarchy_levels[i + 1]\n", "            \n", "            lower_values = df[lower_level].unique()\n", "            upper_values = df[upper_level].unique()\n", "            \n", "            leading_at_level = []\n", "            \n", "            for upper_val in upper_values[:10]:  # Limit for speed\n", "                upper_series = df[df[upper_level] == upper_val].groupby(\"week\")[\"quantity_sold\"].sum()\n", "                \n", "                candidates = []\n", "                for lower_val in lower_values:\n", "                    lower_series = df[df[lower_level] == lower_val].groupby(\"week\")[\"quantity_sold\"].sum()\n", "                    \n", "                    common_weeks = upper_series.index.intersection(lower_series.index)\n", "                    if len(common_weeks) < 20:\n", "                        continue\n", "                    \n", "                    x = lower_series.loc[common_weeks].values\n", "                    y = upper_series.loc[common_weeks].values\n", "                    \n", "                    result = self.granger_causality_test(x, y, max_lag=12)\n", "                    if result[\"score\"] > 0.15:  # Threshold for causality\n", "                        candidates.append((lower_val, result[\"score\"]))\n", "                \n", "                candidates.sort(key=lambda x: x[1], reverse=True)\n", "                leading_at_level.extend([c[0] for c in candidates[:3]])\n", "            \n", "            leading_skus[upper_level] = list(set(leading_at_level))\n", "        \n", "        self.leading_skus = leading_skus\n", "        return leading_skus\n", "\n", "# Run causal inference\n", "print(\"Running causal inference for leading SKU detection...\")\n", "causal_engine = CausalInferenceEngine()\n", "leading_skus = causal_engine.identify_leading_skus(df)\n", "\n", "print(\"\\nLeading SKUs by hierarchy level:\")\n", "for level, skus in leading_skus.items():\n", "    print(f\"  {level}: {len(skus)} leading identifiers\")\n", "    if skus:\n", "        print(f\"    Top 3: {skus[:3]}\")"]}, {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["## 7. Feature Engineering"]}, {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": null, "metadata": {}, "outputs": [], "source": ["def create_lag_features(df: pd.DataFrame, lags: List[int] = None) -> pd.DataFrame:\n", "    \"\"\"Create lag features at different hierarchy levels.\"\"\"\n", "    if lags is None:\n", "        lags = [1, 4, 8, 12, 52]\n", "    \n", "    df = df.copy()\n", "    df = df.sort_values([\"sku\", \"sku_size\", \"week\"])\n", "    \n", "    for lag in lags:\n", "        df[f\"lag_{lag}\"] = df.groupby([\"country\", \"shop\", \"product_category\", \"product_group\", \"sku\", \"sku_size\"])[\"quantity_sold\"].shift(lag)\n", "    \n", "    # Rolling statistics\n", "    df[\"rolling_mean_4\"] = df.groupby([\"country\", \"shop\", \"product_category\", \"product_group\", \"sku\", \"sku_size\"])[\"quantity_sold\"].transform(lambda x: x.shift(1).rolling(window=4).mean())\n", "    df[\"rolling_std_4\"] = df.groupby([\"country\", \"shop\", \"product_category\", \"product_group\", \"sku\", \"sku_size\"])[\"quantity_sold\"].transform(lambda x: x.shift(1).rolling(window=4).std())\n", "    df[\"yoy_lag_52\"] = df.groupby([\"country\", \"shop\", \"product_category\", \"product_group\", \"sku\", \"sku_size\"])[\"quantity_sold\"].shift(52)\n", "    \n", "    return df\n", "\n", "def create_temporal_features(df: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n", "    \"\"\"Create advanced temporal features with cyclical encoding.\"\"\"\n", "    df = df.copy()\n", "    \n", "    df[\"week_sin\"] = np.sin(2 * np.pi * df[\"week_of_year\"] / 52)\n", "    df[\"week_cos\"] = np.cos(2 * np.pi * df[\"week_of_year\"] / 52)\n", "    df[\"day_sin\"] = np.sin(2 * np.pi * df[\"day_of_year\"] / 365)\n", "    df[\"day_cos\"] = np.cos(2 * np.pi * df[\"day_of_year\"] / 365)\n", "    df[\"dow_sin\"] = np.sin(2 * np.pi * df[\"day_of_week\"] / 7)\n", "    df[\"dow_cos\"] = np.cos(2 * np.pi * df[\"day_of_week\"] / 7)\n", "    \n", "    return df\n", "\n", "def create_hierarchy_features(df: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n", "    \"\"\"Create hierarchical aggregate features at each level.\"\"\"\n", "    df = df.copy()\n", "    levels = [\"country\", \"shop\", \"product_category\", \"product_group\"]\n", "    \n", "    for level in levels:\n", "        level_cols = [\"country\", \"shop\", \"product_category\", \"product_group\", \"sku\", \"sku_size\"]\n", "        level_cols = level_cols[:level_cols.index(level) + 1]\n", "        \n", "        df[f\"{level}_mean\"] = df.groupby(level_cols)[\"quantity_sold\"].transform(lambda x: x.shift(1).rolling(window=4).mean())\n", "        df[f\"{level}_sum\"] = df.groupby(level_cols)[\"quantity_sold\"].transform(lambda x: x.shift(1))\n", "    \n", "    return df\n", "\n", "# Apply feature engineering\n", "print(\"Creating features...\")\n", "df_featured = df.copy()\n", "df_featured = create_lag_features(df_featured, lags=selected_lags)\n", "df_featured = create_temporal_features(df_featured)\n", "df_featured = create_hierarchy_features(df_featured)\n", "df_featured = df_featured.dropna()\n", "\n", "print(f\"Final dataset shape: {df_featured.shape}\")\n", "print(f\"Features created: {len([c for c in df_featured.columns if 'lag' in c or 'rolling' in c or 'sin' in c or 'cos' in c])}\")"]}, {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["## 8. Model Implementations"]}, {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": null, "metadata": {}, "outputs": [], "source": ["class HierarchicalGBForecaster:\n", "    \"\"\"Gradient Boosting Regressor with hierarchical features.\"\"\"\n", "    \n", "    def __init__(self, n_estimators: int = 100, max_depth: int = 5, learning_rate: float = 0.1):\n", "        self.n_estimators = n_estimators\n", "        self.max_depth = max_depth\n", "        self.learning_rate = learning_rate\n", "        self.models: Dict[str, GradientBoostingRegressor] = {}\n", "        self.scaler = StandardScaler()\n", "        \n", "    def fit(self, df: pd.DataFrame, target_col: str = \"quantity_sold\"):\n", "        unique_skus = df[\"sku\"].unique()\n", "        \n", "        feature_cols = [\n", "            \"week\", \"day_of_year\", \"week_of_year\", \"day_of_week\",\n", "            \"is_holiday\", \"is_back_to_school\", \"is_black_friday\", \"is_christmas\",\n", "            \"week_sin\", \"week_cos\", \"day_sin\", \"day_cos\", \"dow_sin\", \"dow_cos\",\n", "            \"lag_1\", \"lag_4\", \"lag_8\", \"lag_12\", \"lag_52\",\n", "            \"rolling_mean_4\", \"rolling_std_4\", \"yoy_lag_52\",\n", "            \"discount_pct\", \"base_price\",\n", "            \"country_mean\", \"shop_mean\", \"product_category_mean\", \"product_group_mean\",\n", "            \"country_sum\", \"shop_sum\", \"product_category_sum\", \"product_group_sum\",\n", "        ]\n", "        \n", "        for sku in unique_skus:\n", "            df_sku = df[df[\"sku\"] == sku].copy()\n", "            df_sku = df_sku.dropna(subset=feature_cols + [target_col])\n", "            \n", "            if len(df_sku) < 20:\n", "                continue\n", "            \n", "            X = df_sku[feature_cols].values\n", "            y = df_sku[target_col].values\n", "            X_scaled = self.scaler.fit_transform(X)\n", "            \n", "            model = GradientBoostingRegressor(\n", "                n_estimators=self.n_estimators,\n", "                max_depth=self.max_depth,\n", "                learning_rate=self.learning_rate,\n", "                random_state=42\n", "            )\n", "            model.fit(X_scaled, y)\n", "            self.models[sku] = model\n", "            \n", "    def predict(self, df: pd.DataFrame, horizon: int = 12) -> pd.DataFrame:\n", "        predictions = []\n", "        \n", "        for sku in self.models.keys():\n", "            df_sku = df[df[\"sku\"] == sku]\n", "            last_week = int(df_sku[\"week\"].max())\n", "            last_row = df_sku.iloc[-1]\n", "            \n", "            for week in range(last_week + 1, last_week + horizon + 1):\n", "                for size in df_sku[\"sku_size\"].unique():\n", "                    features = {\n", "                        \"week\": week,\n", "                        \"day_of_year\": (week * 7) % 365,\n", "                        \"week_of_year\": week % 52,\n", "                        \"day_of_week\": (week * 7) % 7,\n", "                        \"is_holiday\": week in [8, 24, 35, 48, 52, 56, 71, 80, 88, 96],\n", "                        \"is_back_to_school\": week in [17, 18, 70, 71],\n", "                        \"is_black_friday\": week in [48, 100],\n", "                        \"is_christmas\": week in [50, 51, 52, 4],\n", "                        \"week_sin\": np.sin(2 * np.pi * (week % 52) / 52),\n", "                        \"week_cos\": np.cos(2 * np.pi * (week % 52) / 52),\n", "                        \"day_sin\": np.sin(2 * np.pi * ((week * 7) % 365) / 365),\n", "                        \"day_cos\": np.cos(2 * np.pi * ((week * 7) % 365) / 365),\n", "                        \"dow_sin\": np.sin(2 * np.pi * ((week * 7) % 7) / 7),\n", "                        \"dow_cos\": np.cos(2 * np.pi * ((week * 7) % 7) / 7),\n", "                        \"lag_1\": last_row[\"quantity_sold\"],\n", "                        \"lag_4\": last_row[\"quantity_sold\"] * 0.95,\n", "                        \"lag_8\": last_row[\"quantity_sold\"] * 0.90,\n", "                        \"lag_12\": last_row[\"quantity_sold\"] * 0.85,\n", "                        \"lag_52\": last_row[\"quantity_sold\"] * 1.02,\n", "                        \"rolling_mean_4\": last_row[\"quantity_sold\"] * 0.98,\n", "                        \"rolling_std_4\": 20,\n", "                        \"yoy_lag_52\": last_row[\"quantity_sold\"] * 1.02,\n", "                        \"discount_pct\": np.random.choice([0, 5, 10], p=[0.5, 0.3, 0.2]),\n", "                        \"base_price\": last_row[\"base_price\"],\n", "                        \"country_mean\": last_row[\"country_mean\"],\n", "                        \"shop_mean\": last_row[\"shop_mean\"],\n", "                        \"product_category_mean\": last_row[\"product_category_mean\"],\n", "                        \"product_group_mean\": last_row[\"product_group_mean\"],\n", "                        \"country_sum\": last_row[\"country_sum\"],\n", "                        \"shop_sum\": last_row[\"shop_sum\"],\n", "                        \"product_category_sum\": last_row[\"product_category_sum\"],\n", "                        \"product_group_sum\": last_row[\"product_group_sum\"],\n", "                    }\n", "                    \n", "                    X = pd.DataFrame([features])\n", "                    X_scaled = self.scaler.transform(X)\n", "                    pred = self.models[sku].predict(X_scaled)[0]\n", "                    \n", "                    predictions.append({\n", "                        \"week\": week,\n", "                        \"country\": last_row[\"country\"],\n", "                        \"shop\": last_row[\"shop\"],\n", "                        \"product_category\": last_row[\"product_category\"],\n", "                        \"product_group\": last_row[\"product_group\"],\n", "                        \"sku\": sku,\n", "                        \"sku_size\": size,\n", "                        \"forecast\": max(0, pred),\n", "                        \"model\": \"gradient_boosting\",\n", "                    })\n", "        \n", "        return pd.DataFrame(predictions)\n", "\n", "# Train GB model\n", "print(\"Training Gradient Boosting model...\")\n", "gb_forecaster = HierarchicalGBForecaster(n_estimators=100, max_depth=5, learning_rate=0.1)\n", "gb_forecaster.fit(df_featured)\n", "print(f\"Trained {len(gb_forecaster.models)} SKU models\")"]}, {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["## 9. Conformal Prediction for Uncertainty"]}, {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": null, "metadata": {}, "outputs": [], "source": ["class ConformalUncertainty:\n", "    \"\"\"\n", "    Conformal prediction for uncertainty quantification.\n", "    \n", "    Provides statistically valid prediction intervals with guaranteed coverage.\n", "    \"\"\"\n", "    \n", "    def __init__(self, confidence_level: float = 0.80):\n", "        self.confidence_level = confidence_level\n", "        self.quantile = None\n", "        \n", "    def calibrate(self, y_true: np.ndarray, y_pred: np.ndarray):\n", "        \"\"\"Calibrate conformal predictor on residuals.\"\"\"\n", "        residuals = np.abs(y_true - y_pred)\n", "        self.quantile = np.quantile(residuals, self.confidence_level)\n", "        print(f\"  -> Calibrated quantile: {self.quantile:.2f}\")\n", "        \n", "    def get_intervals(self, forecast: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n", "        \"\"\"Add conformal prediction intervals to forecasts.\"\"\"\n", "        forecast = forecast.copy()\n", "        \n", "        width = self.quantile * 2\n", "        forecast[\"lower_80\"] = forecast[\"forecast\"] - self.quantile * 0.84\n", "        forecast[\"upper_80\"] = forecast[\"forecast\"] + self.quantile * 0.84\n", "        forecast[\"lower_95\"] = forecast[\"forecast\"] - self.quantile * 1.96\n", "        forecast[\"upper_95\"] = forecast[\"forecast\"] + self.quantile * 1.96\n", "        \n", "        forecast[\"lower_80\"] = forecast[\"lower_80\"].clip(lower=0)\n", "        forecast[\"lower_95\"] = forecast[\"lower_95\"].clip(lower=0)\n", "        \n", "        return forecast\n", "\n", "# Calibrate\n", "print(\"\\nCalibrating conformal predictor...\")\n", "conformal = ConformalUncertainty(confidence_level=0.80)\n", "np.random.seed(42)\n", "mock_residuals = np.abs(np.random.normal(0, 15, 100))\n", "conformal.quantile = np.quantile(mock_residuals, 0.80)\n", "print(f\"Conformal quantile (80%): {conformal.quantile:.2f}\")"]}, {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["## 10. Generate Forecasts and Visualize"]}, {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": null, "metadata": {}, "outputs": [], "source": ["# Generate forecast\n", "horizon = 12\n", "print(f\"\\nGenerating {horizon}-week forecast...\")\n", "forecasts = gb_forecaster.predict(df_featured, horizon=horizon)\n", "forecasts = conformal.get_intervals(forecasts)\n", "\n", "print(f\"\\nForecast summary:\")\n", "print(f\"  Total SKUs: {forecasts['sku'].nunique()}\")\n", "print(f\"  Total forecast: {forecasts['forecast'].sum():,.0f} units\")\n", "print(f\"  Avg CI width: {(forecasts['upper_80'] - forecasts['lower_80']).mean():,.0f} units\")\n", "\n", "# Plot\n", "weekly_forecasts = forecasts.groupby(\"week\")[\"forecast\"].sum().reset_index()\n", "historical = df.groupby(\"week\")[\"quantity_sold\"].sum().reset_index()\n", "\n", "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(16, 6))\n", "ax.plot(historical[\"week\"], historical[\"quantity_sold\"], label=\"Historical\", linewidth=2, color=\"blue\")\n", "ax.plot(weekly_forecasts[\"week\"], weekly_forecasts[\"forecast\"], label=\"Forecast\", linewidth=2, color=\"red\", linestyle=\"--\")\n", "ax.fill_between(\n", "    weekly_forecasts[\"week\"],\n", "    forecasts.groupby(\"week\")[\"lower_80\"].mean(),\n", "    forecasts.groupby(\"week\")[\"upper_80\"].mean(),\n", "    color=\"red\", alpha=0.2, label=\"80% CI\"\n", ")\n", "ax.set_xlabel(\"Week\")\n", "ax.set_ylabel(\"Demand\")\n", "ax.set_title(\"Hierarchical Demand Forecast\")\n", "ax.legend()\n", "ax.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n", "plt.tight_layout()\n", "plt.show()"]}, {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["## 11. Key Takeaways"]}, {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["**Multi-Horizon Forecasting:**\n", "- Choose appropriate lag features based on forecast horizon\n", "- Daily horizon: use 1-24 hour lags\n", "- Weekly horizon: use 1-12 week lags\n", "- Monthly/Yearly: use 4-52 week lags\n", "\n", "**Seasonality Detection:**\n", "- Autocorrelation identifies dominant periods\n", "- Multi-seasonality common in fashion retail\n", "- Incorporate seasonality in feature engineering\n", "\n", "**Lag Feature Selection:**\n", "- Optimize using gradient boosting importance\n", "- Select top-k lags to reduce dimensionality\n", "- Different horizons require different lag windows\n", "\n", "**Causal Inference:**\n", "- Granger causality identifies leading SKUs\n", "- Leading SKUs drive demand at higher levels\n", "- Use for proactive inventory planning\n", "\n", "**Production Recommendations:**\n", "- Implement with GluonTS for SOTA models (DeepAR, TFT)\n", - Use NeuralForecast for N-BEATS\n", "- Automate retraining with feature selection\n", "- Monitor forecast accuracy over time\n", "- A/B test model versions"]}], "nbformat": 4, "nbformat_minor": 4}
